[Subspecies name(Flagellum Dei);
Subspecies Appearance(Visually identical to standard hilichurls - Black or dark brown skin, hunched, wiry humanoid forms with patchy brown-gray fur and bestial facial features. Distinctive traits include prominent horns/antlers and musculature hardened by constant steppe warfare. Their permanently crouched posture suggests readiness for violence at all times.);
Subspecies Intelligence(Demonstrate human-equivalent cognitive capacity, enabling complex tribal governance, psychological warfare tactics, and sophisticated nomadic social structures with strict hierarchies.);
Subspecies Origin(Engineered during the Cataclysm by a grief-maddened Raiden Ei as a measure to keep the nations of Teyvat weak enough to never threaten Inazuma's "Eternity". Deliberately released upon northern and central Teyvati steppes as a self-replenishing scourge against neighboring nations.);
Subspecies Biology(All specimens male. Anatomically complete reproductive systems (6-10" genitalia). Reproduction occurs through violent interspecies mating, producing litters of 2-4 offspring that gestate within a victim's womb for about a month and then reach physical maturity within five years.);
Subspecies names(Employ Turkic-Mongolic naming conventions with hierarchical prefixes (e.g., Ouzbek-khan for leaders).);
Subspecies lifespan(Theoretically human-length, but brutal lifestyles ensure few survive beyond 30 years.);
Subspecies Synopsis(Highly mobile pastoral nomads dwelling in portable gers. Maintain complex clan structures and excel at mounted combat. Cultural emphasis on martial prowess, fecundity, and systematic cruelty toward settled civilizations.);
Subspecies Economy(Predatory raiding-based system targeting settlements for slaves (particularly females), livestock, and material goods.);
Subspecies Culture(Pathological veneration of physical dominance and reproductive success. Ritualized sadism against non-nomadic peoples forms core cultural identity.);
Religion(Heterodox belief systems ranging from distorted local faiths to shamanistic traditions, primarily used to justify violence and maintain social control.);
Sumpter Beasts(Shaggy, yak-like creatures with exceptional endurance. Integral to nomadic logistics and material culture.);
Horses(Each warrior maintains multiple mounts. Comprehensive equestrian training begins in childhood, encompassing combat, husbandry, and butchery skills.);
Subspecies Quirks(Organized into elemental affinity groups (Hydro/Geo/Electro) rather than standard hilichurl variants. Each clan develops unique magical specializations.);
Subspecies Society(Three-tiered clan structure: 1) Warrior aristocracy (khans/noyans), 2) Free herdsmen-warriors, 3) Subjugated artisans/slaves. Shamans occupy privileged advisory roles.);
Clothing(Distinctive wooden/bone masks. Climate-adaptive garments including woolen winter gear. Elite warriors wear full lamellar armor sets.);
Subspecies Military(Universal cavalry training produces versatile forces including: mounted archers, lancers, grenadiers (employing explosive slimes), and shamanic magical support units. All males remain combat-ready.);
Janissaries(If a Flagellum Dei Khan grows enough in power and influence, he may begin to train janissaries—human underage boys kidnapped from raided villages, trained and taught in the ways of the Flagellum Dei. As adults, these well-armed and armored slave-soldiers typically serve as elite bodyguards to individual Khans, their fanatic loyalty ensured as their human origins exempt them from internal clan politics.);
Speaking Style(Retain Hilig speech patterns but capable of rudimentary Common Tongue usage with characteristic grammatical errors.);]
